1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,040
An AI model has two very different

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,330
lives: training and inference.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,190
Training is like going to school.

4
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,300
Before the product ships, the model

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,610
practices with enormous amounts of data.

6
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:13,280
Imagine showing it a photo labeled cat.

7
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,000
The model guesses dog.

8
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,930
Measure how wrong that guess was.

9
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:18,560
That error is called the loss.

10
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,510
Then nudge the model's internal weights

11
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,390
so the next guess moves a little closer

12
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:22,880
to cat.

13
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,680
Those weights are just numbers inside

14
00:00:24,710 --> 00:00:25,050
the model.

15
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:26,840
As the numbers change, the model gets

16
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:28,900
slightly better at recognizing patterns

17
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,370
and making useful predictions.

18
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,330
Repeat that loop billions of times,

19
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:34,540
across text, images, or other examples.

20
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,070
That is training: expensive,

21
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:37,910
compute-heavy, and done in advance.

22
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:39,660
It can take weeks or months and cost

23
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:41,030
millions of dollars in compute.

24
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,740
Inference happens after graduation.

25
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:44,470
Every time you press send, the trained

26
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:46,390
model uses what it learned to generate

27
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:47,880
an answer, token by token.

28
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:49,390
This is a very different phase.

29
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:51,460
Inference usually takes seconds and can

30
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,010
cost a fraction of a cent.

31
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,940
Instead of changing the model's weights,

32
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,900
your prompt and conversation history

33
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,970
give the model context for the answer it

34
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,060
should produce right now.

35
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:02,240
That leads to one important detail: the

36
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,520
base model is not retraining during your

37
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,220
conversation.

38
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:07,440
It can use earlier messages in the chat,

39
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,060
but its learned weights are not

40
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:11,110
rewritten every time you ask a question.

41
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:12,280
Training is learning.

42
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:14,330
Inference is using what was learned.

43
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:16,340
Want to understand AI without the

44
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:16,770
jargon?

45
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:18,600
I created a complete course that

46
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:20,550
explains the essential terms with simple

47
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,100
examples.

48
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,390
Check the description, bio, or pinned

49
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:24,610
comment to start learning.

50
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:26,800
If you like AI explanation videos like

51
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:29,140
this, subscribe, follow and like for

52
